# Code references that no longer exist and shouldn't — checked by
# scripts/check-design-log.mjs. Format: <entry-number> <token> [<token>…]
# Use `*` as the entry number to allow a token everywhere.
#
# Only add a line when the entry is *deliberately* naming something gone —
# a rename record, or a change that got reverted. If the entry still describes
# dead code as though it were live, it needs a supersession note instead.
# Every line here should say which.

# Rename record: "src/lib/homepage-slides.ts → src/lib/history.ts" and
# "Slideshow.astro → HistoryTimeline.astro". Naming the old path is the point.
015 src/lib/homepage-slides.ts src/components/Slideshow.astro

# The entry documents its own reversal: "The src/middleware.ts from this change
# is a no-op, so it was reverted." Exactly what a superseded entry should say.
020 src/middleware.ts

# Addendum 2 documents its own removal: "removed the `>= XL_BREAKPOINT`
# early-return entirely (and the now-unused XL_BREAKPOINT constant)."
048 XL_BREAKPOINT
